      "writtenOn": "2025-01-21T20:02:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I suggest using `void*` and a user provided context object, not a `AVirtualMachine*`. `AVirtualMachine` is opaque, you can\u0027t put a custom context pointer or data in it. If the user wants some kind of closure, they\u0027ll end up needing to use global variables to access it from the callback.\n\nThat also simplifies the implementation, don\u0027t need to make the internals use `Arc`/`Weak`/etc",
      "parentUuid": "1163fb46_81771f31",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 314,
        "startChar": 44,
        "endLine": 314,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "87340e208762cfa3dffd3c73370e801ccd866c6e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c022b672_29d515c8",
        "filename": "libs/libavf/include/android/virtualization.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 314,
      "author": {
        "id": 1019013
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-23T23:50:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, I prefer `AVirtualMachine*` for following reasons:\n  - There\u0027 not much use case of launching various types of VMs.\n  - I expect that the most use case is calling `destroy(vm)`. VM would be sufficient for most cases.\n  - API guide says to accept request identifier when callback can be reused, but this callback is probably not. VM object can\u0027t be restarted, and callback is only set in start()",
      "parentUuid": "d57e5d11_027a1926",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 314,
        "startChar": 44,
        "endLine": 314,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "87340e208762cfa3dffd3c73370e801ccd866c6e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5089e0e6_e0a96069",
        "filename": "libs/libavf/include/android/virtualization.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 314,
      "author": {
        "id": 1944400
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-27T20:16:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e There\u0027 not much use case of launching various types of VMs.\n\nEven if there is only one VM, should we force people to use globals if they need any context besides the `AVirtualMachine*`?\n\n\u003e I expect that the most use case is calling `destroy(vm)`. VM would be sufficient for most cases.\n\nSupporting all use cases is better than only supporting most. A user provided `void*` is completely general, it covers all possible closures.\n\nI think it is OK to provide both the `void*` and the `AVirtualMachine*` and then people can provide `NULL` if they really only need the `AVirtualMachine*`",
      "parentUuid": "c022b672_29d515c8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 314,
        "startChar": 44,
        "endLine": 314,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "87340e208762cfa3dffd3c73370e801ccd866c6e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
